Hot Fill Beverage Co-Packing Services
Big Brands provides Hot Fill Beverage Co-Packing services for our clients from our Southern California plant. Hot Fill is a process that utilizes heat to sterilize the container and the product during the packaging of the beverage product. Hot fill happens when the beverage is heated to a temperature of 194 degrees Farenheit to remove harmful bacteria or microorganisms which may be in products. From there, we place the heated fluid into the glass or PET bottle. After the heat cycle, the filled products and packaging are held for 15-20 seconds at that temperature to ensure there are no bacteria in the product or packaging. From there, the containers rest until the temperature has reached 180 degrees Farenehit. The bottles are then capped and rapidly cooled.
### Cold Fill Beverage Co-Packing Services from Big Brands
Big Brands provides Cold Fill beverage co-packing for our clients. As cold fill beverage copackers, during the cold fill process the container is pressurized by cooling the product then the cold product is added to the cold container. The cold fill process requires sterilization, which can be either a wet or dry sterilization. Cold fill beverage co-packing is a common method for fresh products including juices and dairy products. If you are looking for a Cold Fill beverage copacker or would like more info on the cold fill beverage co-packing process, give the team at Big Brands a call.
